  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788510",
      "title": "Outputting Dynamic Content with String Interpolation",
      "lectureOrder": 22,
      "videoOrder": 19,
      "sourceHash": "f1afa85fba257359f76190266972875dfee1ed36831c5701d2f291365a09b077",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 1.53,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] When it comes to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.53,
          "end": 5.31,
          "en": "outputting dynamic content in Angular applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.31,
          "end": 10.2,
          "en": "you get two main ways of binding your template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.2,
          "end": 12.18,
          "en": "or parts of your template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.18,
          "end": 15.6,
          "en": "two values generated by the component class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 18.903,
          "en": "so to the selected user property, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.19,
          "end": 23.43,
          "en": "And the first way of binding a part of your template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.43,
          "end": 26.763,
          "en": "is by using so-called string interpolation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 29.91,
          "en": "which you do by using two",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.91,
          "end": 33.54,
          "en": "opening and closing curly braces, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.54,
          "end": 36.543,
          "en": "So opening and closing double curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.47,
          "end": 40.14,
          "en": "And then between those curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.14,
          "end": 43.128,
          "en": "you can now reference any public property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.128,
          "end": 46.11,
          "en": "of your component class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.11,
          "end": 48.9,
          "en": "And this is a public property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.9,
          "end": 50.28,
          "en": "You could mark it as private",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.28,
          "end": 52.23,
          "en": "by adding private in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.23,
          "end": 54.93,
          "en": "Then it would not be available in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.93,
          "end": 58.35,
          "en": "It would then only be available within the class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 60.09,
          "en": "But that's not what we want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.09,
          "end": 63.57,
          "en": "So by not adding private, it will automatically be public.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.57,
          "end": 66.84,
          "en": "And therefore in the user component template file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.84,
          "end": 69.99,
          "en": "you can now target selected user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.99,
          "end": 73.17,
          "en": "and you should be getting some IDE support here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.17,
          "end": 75.813,
          "en": "if you're using visuals studio code, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.77,
          "end": 80.1,
          "en": "and then use the dot notation on that property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.1,
          "end": 82.56,
          "en": "because the value stored in that property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.56,
          "end": 84.96000000000001,
          "en": "will be such a user object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.96000000000001,
          "end": 87.96000000000001,
          "en": "Keep in mind that dummy users is an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.96000000000001,
          "end": 90.123,
          "en": "full of objects that look like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.99,
          "end": 94.143,
          "en": "so that have an ID, a name and an avatar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.49000000000001,
          "end": 98.398,
          "en": "And therefore here we can access .name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.398,
          "end": 102.03,
          "en": "And again, you should be getting some IDE support here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.03,
          "end": 106.17,
          "en": "since the IDE, thanks to some tools provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.17,
          "end": 107.7,
          "en": "under the hood by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.7,
          "end": 109.68,
          "en": "understands this connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.68,
          "end": 112.22999999999999,
          "en": "between template and component class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.22999999999999,
          "end": 114.393,
          "en": "and the structure of our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.89,
          "end": 118.83,
          "en": "And this is then how you can output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.83,
          "end": 123.83,
          "en": "dynamic text or dynamic content in general in your templates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.77,
          "end": 128.01,
          "en": "by using this string interpolation feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.01,
          "end": 130.113,
          "en": "with the double curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.09,
          "end": 134.94,
          "en": "If you do that and you save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.94,
          "end": 136.14,
          "en": "you should then see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.14,
          "end": 138.87,
          "en": "that every time you reload this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.87,
          "end": 141,
          "en": "you are seeing a different name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141,
          "end": 143.82,
          "en": "Well, you might sometimes see the same name twice in a row",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.82,
          "end": 145.32,
          "en": "because it is random,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.32,
          "end": 148.203,
          "en": "but it should change fairly frequently.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
